&lt;p&gt;This chapter explores how learners acquire &lt;strong&gt;functional morphology&lt;/strong&gt; (grammatical morphemes like -ing, past tense -ed, 3SG -s) in second language (L2) acquisition. It addresses key questions: Do L2 learners follow fixed acquisition orders? Why do they struggle with morphology even if their syntax is intact? And what theories explain these challenges?&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Ch.8: Acquisition of Syntax</title><link>https://zjpsycholin.github.io/SLA4pg/chapter8/</link><pubDate>Sun, 20 Apr 2025 16:45:00 -0400</pubDate><guid>https://zjpsycholin.github.io/SLA4pg/chapter8/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="chapter-8--acquisition-of-syntax"&gt;
