&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This chapter explores the acquisition of &lt;strong&gt;syntax&lt;/strong&gt; (sentence structure and grammatical dependencies) in second language (L2) learning, with a focus on three core themes: how the concept of &amp;ldquo;syntactic parameters&amp;rdquo; has evolved, whether L2 learners develop native-like syntactic representations, and how cross-linguistic differences (e.g., word order, verb movement, wh-movement) shape acquisition.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Ch.10: Acquisition of the Syntax-Semantics Interface</title><link>https://zjpsycholin.github.io/SLA4pg/chapter10/</link><pubDate>Sun, 04 May 2025 17:15:00 -0400</pubDate><guid>https://zjpsycholin.github.io/SLA4pg/chapter10/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="chapter-10--acquisition-of-the-syntax-semantics-interface"&gt;
 Chapter 10 — Acquisition of the Syntax-Semantics Interface
